WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.163 --> 00:00:01.690
(gentle playful music)

00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.413
- [Narrator] This is the
mossy frog, a tiny amphibian,

00:00:04.413 --> 00:00:07.240
found predominantly
within the flooded caves

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:09.111
of northern Vietnam's forests.

00:00:09.111 --> 00:00:10.747
Its main mode of defense,

00:00:10.747 --> 00:00:13.023
you're looking at it.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.204
The mossy frog's skin is
a blotchy green and brown,

00:00:20.204 --> 00:00:22.872
a perfect color match
for the mossy environment

00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:24.430
it's found in.

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.553
If threatened, it will
curl up and play dead

00:00:26.553 --> 00:00:28.787
to hide from possible predators.

00:00:28.787 --> 00:00:31.847
They are semi-aquatic,
and the suction-like discs

00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:35.210
at the end of its toes
make it an agile climber

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:36.673
when out of the water.

00:00:36.673 --> 00:00:39.650
For food, they are opportunistic,

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.790
meaning they'll feed on
anything available to them,

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:44.622
as their habitat goes
through constant change.

00:00:44.622 --> 00:00:47.723
One change in particular
is the recent deforestation

00:00:47.723 --> 00:00:50.260
of northern Vietnam's forests.

00:00:50.260 --> 00:00:52.116
As the forests have become smaller,

00:00:52.116 --> 00:00:54.980
so has the mossy frog's population,

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:58.028
landing them on the
endangered species list.

00:00:58.028 --> 00:01:00.203
This is the mossy frog.

00:01:05.211 --> 00:01:07.128
(ding)

